      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6rv",
          "text": "Being involved in a car accident can be a terrifying experience, but ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6rw",
          "text": "leaving the scene of an accident in Colorado",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6rx",
          "text": " can lead to serious repercussions. Colorado law imposes strict penalties on drivers who don’t stay at the scene, with consequences that may include a Class 2 misdemeanor for property damage or felony charges when someone is hurt or killed. A conviction might also result in the suspension of your driver’s license, adding to the challenges you’ll face afterward. What you do in the moments after a crash can shape the legal path ahead.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
