        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6s9",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6s8",
          "text": "What Is a Hit-and-Run Car Accident in Colorado?",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6sb",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6sa",
          "text": "A hit-and-run occurs when a driver in an accident fails to fulfill their legal obligations before leaving the scene. Under Colorado law, drivers must stop, assist if needed, and exchange information with other parties involved. It doesn’t matter if the accident involves other vehicles, cyclists, pedestrians, or property; leaving without fulfilling these duties constitutes a hit-and-run.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6sd",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6sc",
          "text": "Reasons drivers may flee the scene include panic, lack of a valid driver’s license, driving under the influence, or fear of legal and financial repercussions. Regardless of the reasons, leaving the scene violates Colorado Revised Statutes and can lead to significant penalties.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6sf",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6se",
          "text": "What Should You Do After a Car Accident or Hit-and-Run?",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6sk",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l6sh",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://colorado.public.law/statutes/crs_42-4-1603"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6sg",
          "text": "Under ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6si",
          "text": "Colorado Law",
          "marks": [
            "l6sh"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6sj",
          "text": ", you’re legally required to stop and provide aid or information if you’re involved in an accident, regardless of fault.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6sm",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6sl",
          "text": "1. Ensure Safety",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6so",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6sn",
          "text": "If the accident happened in a high-traffic area, move yourself and your vehicle to a safe spot when possible. Check on your own condition and others.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6sq",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6sp",
          "text": "2. Call 911",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6ss",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6sr",
          "text": "Report the crash to the police, especially when injuries or visible damage are involved. Give them your precise location and explain what happened.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6su",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6st",
          "text": "3. Exchange Information",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6sw",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6sv",
          "text": "When it’s safe to do so, share your full name, address, phone number, insurance details, and license plate with the other party involved in the crash.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6sy",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6sx",
          "text": "4. Gather Evidence",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6t0",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6sz",
          "text": "Use your phone to photograph the accident scene. Focus on the vehicles involved, visible damage, skid marks, and traffic signs.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6t2",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6t1",
          "text": "5. Locate Witnesses",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6t4",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6t3",
          "text": "If bystanders saw what happened, kindly ask for their contact information.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6t6",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6t5",
          "text": "6. Report to Your Insurance Company",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6t8",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6t7",
          "text": "Let your insurer know about the accident right away, even if you weren’t at fault or the other driver fled the scene.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6ta",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6t9",
          "text": "7. File a Police Report",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6te",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l6tb",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://www.dmv.org/co-colorado/accident-guide/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6tc",
          "text": "Colorado law",
          "marks": [
            "l6tb"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6td",
          "text": " requires accident reporting. If officers don’t respond to the scene, you can file a report online through the Department of Revenue.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6tg",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6tf",
          "text": "8. Seek Medical Attention",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6ti",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6th",
          "text": "Visit a doctor to make sure you didn’t suffer hidden trauma like concussions or internal damage.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6tk",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6tj",
          "text": "9. Consider Legal Counsel",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6tm",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6tl",
          "text": "In a serious injury or a hit-and-run case, it’s wise to speak with a Colorado car accident attorney who can help you through the legal process.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6to",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6tn",
          "text": "Is Leaving the Scene of an Accident Illegal in Colorado?",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6tq",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6tp",
          "text": "Yes, leaving the scene of an accident is illegal in Colorado. Whether the incident involves injury, death, or property damage, Colorado Revised Statutes mandate specific actions from all drivers involved.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6ts",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6tr",
          "text": "Breaking these laws can lead to criminal charges that vary in severity depending on the circumstances:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6tv",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6tt",
          "text": "Class 2 Misdemeanor Traffic Offense",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6tu",
          "text": " if the accident resulted only in property damage, such as damage to vehicles or other property.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6ty",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6tw",
          "text": "Class 1 Misdemeanor Traffic Offense",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6tx",
          "text": " if the accident caused injuries to one or more individuals.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6u1",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6tz",
          "text": "Felony Charges",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6u0",
          "text": " are imposed if the accident caused severe injuries or resulted in fatalities, with more serious legal consequences.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6u3",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6u2",
          "text": "The severity and classification of charges depend on factors like the outcome of the accident, prior offenses, and whether the driver was impaired.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6u5",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6u4",
          "text": "Consequences of a Hit-and-Run Accident in Colorado",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6u7",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6u6",
          "text": "Leaving the scene of an accident has wide-reaching consequences, both legally and personally. These include:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6u9",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6u8",
          "text": "Legal Penalties",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6ud",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l6ua",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "/what-is-the-statute-of-limitations-for-hit-and-run-in-colorado/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6ub",
          "text": "Hit-and-run accidents",
          "marks": [
            "l6ua"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6uc",
          "text": " are serious crimes with severe legal consequences. Depending on the case, convicted drivers may face fines, jail time, or the loss of their driver’s license. These charges often lead to a permanent criminal record, limiting future opportunities like employment, housing, or professional licensing. Repeat offenders may face harsher penalties, including longer prison sentences.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6uf",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6ue",
          "text": "Financial Repercussions",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6uh",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6ug",
          "text": "The financial impact of a hit-and-run can be overwhelming. Courts typically hold fleeing drivers responsible for all damages, including medical bills, property repairs, and potentially punitive damages for reckless behavior. Drivers may also face higher insurance premiums or risk losing coverage altogether.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6uj",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6ui",
          "text": "Emotional and Social Costs",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6ul",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6uk",
          "text": "Leaving the scene of an accident has lasting emotional and social consequences. It damages public trust and personal relationships, as others may consider the driver irresponsible. For victims, a hit-and-run can cause lifelong trauma, from physical injuries and emotional distress to a lingering sense of injustice. These effects ripple through families, communities, and society, undermining trust and safety on the roads.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6un",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6um",
          "text": "Penalties for Leaving the Scene of an Accident in Colorado",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6ur",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6uo",
          "text": "The penalties for ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6up",
          "text": "leaving the scene of an accident in Colorado",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6uq",
          "text": " (hit-and-run) depend on how severe the crash is. If only property damage occurred, it’s treated as a Class 2 misdemeanor. When someone is hurt, the consequences grow more severe. If a fatality happens, the driver could be charged with a Class 3 felony.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6ut",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6us",
          "text": "The Importance of Legal Representation in Hit-and-Run Cases",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6uv",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6uu",
          "text": "If you are facing accusations of leaving the scene or are a victim of a hit-and-run accident, contacting an attorney should be a priority. A knowledgeable legal team can provide guidance, protect your rights, and help manage the legal complexities of your situation.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6ux",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6uw",
          "text": "For those facing charges, seasoned counsel can reduce penalties by highlighting mitigating factors. On the other hand, if you’re a victim, an attorney can help secure compensation for medical expenses, property repairs, and emotional distress.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
